#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:1
msgid "ADR-0021: Public API and stability of LUMOS 1.x"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-18"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P15.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:9
msgid ""
"LUMOS 1.0 freezes its API and its `.lumos` format (plan, P15.1). Users "
"write scripts and notebooks, save `.lumos` files, call the HTTP API and "
"let assistants call the MCP tools; all of them must keep working through "
"the 1.x versions. The review of the API before the freeze found few "
"inconsistencies: two settings and one function spelled in British English"
" (`normalise`, `subaperture_centres`) among American identifiers "
"(`normalize`, `center`, `polarization`, `colorbar`), an element class "
"named differently from its type (`PSFMeasurementElement` for "
"`lumos.processing.PSFMeasurement`), 110 fields of element types without "
"description, two subpackages without `__all__` and two absent from the "
"API reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:17
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:19
msgid "**What is public** in 1.x, and covered by the rules below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:20
msgid ""
"the names listed in `__all__` of `lumos` and of its public subpackages "
"(`backend`, `catalogs`, `core`, `elements`, `fields`, `hardware`, `io`, "
"`plotting`, `processing`, `propagation`, `results`, `scenes`, `service`, "
"`symbolic`) and documented in the API reference;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:23
msgid ""
"the element types: their identifiers `lumos.<family>.<ClassName>`, fields"
" (names, kinds, units) and ports;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:24
msgid "the `.lumos` format 1.x and its JSON schema;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:25
msgid ""
"the models of the service layer, the routes of the HTTP API, the MCP "
"tools and their arguments, the commands of the `lumos` command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:28
msgid ""
"Names starting with `_`, `lumos._vendor`, the internals of `lumos.web` "
"(other than `create_app` and its configuration) and the web interface "
"itself are not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:30
msgid ""
"**Semantic versioning**: a 1.x release adds and fixes, it does not remove"
" or rename. A public name to be removed is deprecated first "
"(`DeprecationWarning`, documented in the changelog) during at least one "
"minor release, and removed in 2.0 at the earliest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:33
msgid ""
"**Element types and files**: a change of the fields of an element type "
"raises its type version and adds a migration (`registry.add_migration`), "
"so that every `.lumos` file written by a 1.x version is read by the later"
" ones. A new feature of the format raises its minor version (1.1 added "
"the feedbacks, ADR-0020): newer readers read older documents; older "
"readers refuse newer ones with a clear error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:37
msgid ""
"**Conventions of the identifiers**: snake_case; American spelling, as "
"NumPy, astropy and matplotlib (`normalize`, `center`, `color`, "
"`polarization`), the prose of the documentation being free; physical "
"quantities as `astropy.units.Quantity`; counts named `n_<things>`; every "
"field of an element type has a short description (shown by the web "
"interface, the JSON schemas and the MCP server)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:41
msgid ""
"The review renames, before the freeze: the setting `normalise` of "
"`FlatField` and `KernelObservables` and the keyword of `flat_field` and "
"`kernel_observables` (type version 2, documents of version 1 migrated); "
"`subaperture_centres` to `subaperture_centers`; the element class "
"`PSFMeasurementElement` to `PSFMeasurement` (its type identifier) and the"
" result of `measure_psf` from `PSFMeasurement` to `PSFResult`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:46
msgid ""
"`tests/unit/test_api_review.py` checks points 1 and 4 (documentation of "
"the element types, identifiers, spelling, `__all__`, API reference) at "
"every run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:49
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:51
msgid ""
"British spelling everywhere: most identifiers and the scientific Python "
"ecosystem are American; renaming `polarization`, `center` and `colorbar` "
"would break more than it fixes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:53
msgid ""
"Aliases keeping the old spellings: LUMOS was not released yet (0.x); "
"migrations of the type versions keep the files readable, which is what "
"matters to users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:56
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:58
msgid ""
"Users of 1.x can rely on the public API and on their files; the changelog"
" lists every deprecation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:59
msgid ""
"New element types and fields must follow the conventions, or the review "
"test fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0021-api-stability.md:60
msgid "Adding to the format needs an ADR and a minor version of the format."
msgstr ""

